-## Adopted action-proof lesson — video 002
+## References and adoption
 
-The user liked video 002's complete-character eight-second run/jump review and explicitly asked to preserve the approach for future projects. Use [whole-character action blocking](../../pipeline/motion-planning.md#reusable-whole-character-action-proof) as a starting option: coherent matching action drawings, readable opposite strides, preparation/flight/contact/recovery, editable pose exposure and travel. Preserve video 001's head/body/kit/boots quality as the local visual floor. Keep body travel and camera separate from drawing registration; inspect contacts and temporal stability in the rendered action. [v003 and its evidence](videos/002-how-arsenal-won-the-league/artifacts/pose-action-v003/README.md) preserve the liked poses while correcting the measured jitter. The user subsequently accepted v003's running/jumping as almost perfect and better than video001, authorizing adaptation to Gyökeres. New adaptations retain their own review. This does not automatically approve new characters, views or future films.
