-### Football environment continuity
-
-For pitch action, reuse the dimensional field/goal mechanism demonstrated in video 001, adapting location identity to the current film. Put cast, ball, goal, penalty-area lines, byline, touchline and corner flags in one coordinate system before framing. Establish player/goal scale in a wide view and preserve it through camera cuts; do not independently size a goal to fill spare screen space. A flag belongs at a field corner, not beside the nearest visible goalpost. Use net depth, ground contact shadows, perspective and supporting roles to communicate depth around drawn characters. Review the rendered whole scene as well as character closeups. Video 002 v017 records the implementation and dimensions. On 18 September the user selected its visual direction and requested a dialogue/caption revision; that feedback does not approve future shots or new voices.
-
-### Selected visual recipe — video 002 v017
-
-The user explicitly liked v017’s visual direction. Reuse its complete-character source fitting and dimensional setting as an available baseline: [native scene and implementation record](videos/002-how-arsenal-won-the-league/artifacts/batch02-v017/README.md). Preserve head-to-toe drawing coherence, recognisable likeness, connected clothing, shoes, restrained facial motion, action speed, hand-to-prop contact and spatial scale together. Dialogue changes must not trigger character reconstruction. v018 demonstrates a scoped update of speech timing, mouth animation and captions while retaining that artwork and physical action. The user approved the v018 cut and authorized the next chronological batch on 19 September; that approval does not automatically apply to new shots. Keep the successful Bruno run/jump recipe for demanding action; it complements the source-fitted gesture rig rather than replacing every type of shot.
-
-
-### New match-action transfer checks — video 002 v019
-
-[The v019 record](videos/002-how-arsenal-won-the-league/artifacts/defence-v019/README.md) identifies new-shot failures caught before review: crossing limbs cannot be weighted by a simple left/right x split; wall travel must be split into reachable alternating steps; jump height and flight duration need checking together; copied props must retain physical dimensions after camera-specific scales are removed. Verify these in consecutive rendered contact frames, alongside the existing appearance and voice floor. A standing/gesture drawing has a bounded movement range; use the accepted matched action-drawing approach where that range is exceeded. The user rejected v019’s new-player performance as static. Its technical checks do not establish an accepted acting baseline.
