+# Samtoons reusable evidence and selections v002
+
+22 September 2026. This index adds video 002's useful work and its known limits without duplicating the large assets. [manifest.json](manifest.json) pins workspace-relative source paths, hashes, ownership and review events. [v001](../reuse-v001/README.md) retains the actual selected voice/brand files and provenance. Existing movies, models and selected takes remain intact.
+
+## What can be reused
+
+| Reference | Useful scope | Required limits and next-use work |
+|---|---|---|
+| v001 selected voices and logo | Exact reviewed dialogue takes, character-energy references and channel artwork | Preserve provenance; a new line or performance is a new review. Do not silently select an old voice for the next cast. |
+| Video 001 delivered native scene | Coherent full-body illustration, fitted controls, clothes, shoes and specific reviewed performances | Scene-bound work, not standalone rigs. Identify dependencies and actual collection/control ownership before extraction. Never transfer source thresholds/weights blindly. |
+| Video 002 `opening-motion.blend` / `opening-dialogue.blend` | v017 environment/physical work and v018 character fitting, speech timing and scoped updates | Use the native source map, then author the next scene's performance. The later acting critique applies despite earlier approval. |
+| Video 002 `defence.blend` | Scoped football contacts, spatial scale, wall/cameo relationships and supporting roles | Inspect new body/ball actions, look and cut continuity separately; do not inherit generic choreography. |
+| Video 002 `remaining.blend` | v025 sleeve-to-hand reconstruction, contextual grips/earpiece/button and selected chase/finale work | File contains 30 scenes retaining older names; saved geometry includes later corrections. Open the selected file/scene rather than infer content from a scene suffix. |
+| `pose-action-v003.blend` | Accepted whole-character run/jump and correction of measured temporal jitter | Fixed-view matched drawings with bounded support deformation; not a universal rig, walk cycle or proof of dialogue acting. New characters and views need inspection. |
+| v029 branding scene and rendered segments | Accepted v028 mascot, intro/outro timing and sound, delivered at 1080p | Editable source is scene-bound. Episode paper gag and end-card arrangement are adaptable, not required story elements. |
+
+## Locate the actual selected source
+
+The [video 002 native delivery guide](../../videos/002-how-arsenal-won-the-league/artifacts/delivery-v027/README.md) and its `edit.json` identify native file, scene, local range and film order. The four packed native files preserve the accepted construction. [Branded delivery](../../videos/002-how-arsenal-won-the-league/artifacts/delivery-v029/README.md) adds independent channel segments; it does not contain replacement original-film sources.
+
+Treat those native snapshots as file-owned render inputs. Some authoring scripts depend on live registries and functions from earlier revisions; they are investigation references, not standalone rebuild commands. Read dependencies and destructive operations before reuse. Copy only the needed files into the new film, record source/hash and ownership, then save/reopen and run its intended next operation. Do not overwrite reviewed assets or regenerate accepted voice takes merely because an edit changes timing.
+
+The [Phase A runtime check](../../../../pipeline/revisions/performance-workflow-v002/runtime-check/verify.json) keyed an existing native camera on a copy of `opening-dialogue.blend`, saved/reopened it and rendered the same frame. [Decoded pixels matched](../../../../pipeline/revisions/performance-workflow-v002/runtime-check/comparison.json). This verifies that bounded file-owned correction/render route. It does **not** establish portable character extraction, new expressions, head turns or performance quality.
+
+## Acceptance and known weaknesses stay together
+
+The manifest cites the actual video 002 journal events: the v003 action proof; v025 hand/movement excerpt; complete v026 cut; and v028 branding staging/sound/animatic. v027/v029 exports retain those decisions without inventing new user acceptance. The original v025 README describes its state before the later scoped approval; use the journal events to resolve that chronology.
+
+Later feedback and the [acting diagnosis](../../videos/002-how-arsenal-won-the-league/research/acting-root-cause-and-next-production.md) identify repetitive facing, resting hands, weak expression changes and insufficient reactions. Do not promote these weaknesses as the accepted target. New shots must demonstrate the complete [benchmark](../../benchmark-v003.md) while retaining good identity, connected construction and contact work.
+
+Rejected v019/v020 held-action adaptations, v024 wrist patches and the early rejected chase remain historical failure evidence. A numerical correction or reused rig does not reverse an artistic rejection. No new normal-speed playback, listening or universal-rig validation is claimed by this catalogue.
+
+Use the [production snapshot convention](../../../README.md#shared-assets-and-stable-selections). Reusing a character, set or brand segment does not establish shared plot continuity, and this catalogue does not choose the next story's cast.
